        "answer": 0,
        "why": "Because Cov(L * Z) = L * Cov(Z) * L^T = L * I * L^T = Sigma, multiplying the Cholesky factor L by independent standard normal random variables guarantees that the resulting variables exhibit the exact desired correlation matrix."
